UPDATE "source_value_extractions" SET "notes" = 'MARKED CONTESTED ON AN ADVERSARIAL FINDING, which is the honest state rather than a defended one. The challenge: this source''s own harvested phrases are ''turning diameter'' (obs 6) and ''turning 180 degrees in a corridor'' (obs 7), and its sibling REF-00972 states a 1.5 m TURNING CIRCLE -- so the pair''s subject is arguably TERM-003, not TERM-002, and filing them under corridor width attaches turning-space measurement to a straight-clear-width parameter. What holds the row here: one of the five configurations measured is explicitly a corridor, and the quantity measured for it is the corridor dimension required. What weakens it: the quoted conclusion spans ALL FIVE configurations, not the corridor one alone. REF-00972 was deliberately NOT extracted on this parameter for the same reason -- its 1.5 m figure is a turning circle outright. || 2026-09-13 figure_role SET NULL -> finding (reports that no scooter fits the space existing standards allow; asserts no width itself)', "updated_at" = '2026-09-13 02:52', "updated_by_session" = 'session_2026-09-13-backfill-figure-roles', "figure_role" = 'finding' WHERE "extraction_id" = 6;
